[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:18[39m:

  - A native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so clicking the text toggles it. On/off state is handled by
    the browser — no JS needed.
  - One CSS rule strikes through the label text when checked, so "done" is visible at a glance.

  I used a placeholder item ("Write the thing") since the page has no task data yet. If tasks will come from somewhere
  (a list, a data source, user input), tell me and I'll wire the checkbox into that instead of a hardcoded row.

  No tests run — the repo has no test setup.

